text.en:
Who May File a Complaint. - Complaints on
cases of any form of child sexual abuse or exploitation
punishable under this Act may be filed by the following:
(1) Offended party;
(2) Parents or guardians;
(3) Ascendant or collateral relative within the third (3rd)
degree of consanguinity;
(4) Officer, social worker or representative of a licensed
child-caring institution;
(5) Officer or social worker of the DSWD;
(6) Local social welfare development officer;
(7) Any barangay official;
(8) Any law enforcement officer;
(9) At least three (3) concerned responsible citizens
residing in the place where the violation occurred; or
(10) Any person who has personal knowledge of the
circumstances of the commission of any offense under this Act.
